nd the two keys’ IDs in its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/oid4vcwallet.OID4VCWallet\/documentation\/OID4VCWallet\/InstanceRegistry","isActive":true},{"text":". The registration key signs every later","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"request (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Wallet-Provider-Request"},{"text":"); no attestation names it. If","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the registration, its key or the App Attest key is lost, the next","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Wallet Attestation registers again, with new keys. An App Attest","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"key a registration made but couldn’t register — App Attest’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"server or the provider unavailable, or no connection — is kept, in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"this process, and tried again by the next registration, as Apple","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"asks; it’s dropped when the provider or App Attest refuses it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/oid4vcwallet.OID4VCWallet\/documentation\/OID4VCWallet\/HttpWalletProvider\/walletAttestation(clientID:instanceKey:)","isActive":true},{"text":" asks for a Wallet","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Attestation for the instance key (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"instance_key"},{"text":"). The first time,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it sends an App Attest assertion over a fresh ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"instance"},{"text":" challenge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and the key, which the provider records the key with; once it has,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the key alone — and the assertion again if the provider no longer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"has its record (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"evidence_required"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/oid4vcwallet.OID4VCWallet\/documentation\/OID4VCWallet\/HttpWalletProvider\/keyAttestation(instanceKey:keys:nonce:)","isActive":true},{"text":" asks for a Key","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Attestation over the holder keys, with one assertion over a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"holder"},{"text":" challenge and all of them, for the issuance of its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"instance key, which a Wallet Attestation recorded.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"App Attest attests the app, not the wallet’s keys: the provider"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"learns that a genuine copy of the app on a genuine Apple device asked"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for them, not where they are. Make them in the Secure Enclave all the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/oid4vcwallet.OID4VCWallet\/documentation\/OID4VCWallet\/KeychainKeyStore"},{"type":"text","text":"‘s default). Where App Attest isn’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"supported — the Simulator, some older devices — the wallet can’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"register, and every attestation fails as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".platform"},{"type":"text","text":": there’s no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"unattested path, in development either. A development build (the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"com.apple.developer.devicecheck.appattest-environment"},{"type":"text","text":" entitlement"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"set to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"development"},{"type":"text","text":") makes development-environment keys, which only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a provider configured for them accepts."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Assertions are made one at a time, each sent before the next is made,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as the provider accepts only an assertion whose counter exceeds the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"last it took, and the installation registers once. Every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HttpWalletProvider"},{"type":"text","text":" over the same "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/oid4vcwallet.OID4VCWallet\/documentation\/OID4VCWallet\/FileInstanceRegistry"},{"type":"text","text":" file (or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the same "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/oid4vcwallet.OID4VCWallet\/documentation\/OID4VCWallet\/InMemoryInstanceRegistry"},{"type":"text","text":") in the process shares that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order, so a wallet rebuilt mid-issuance with a new provider is still"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"serialised with the old one. Over a registry of its own type, a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"provider serialises only its own calls: keep one provider for it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It sends nothing but to its base URL, over https, following no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"redirect, with its timeout for each request, and reads at most"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"256 KiB of an answer. It checks a Wallet Attestation is for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"client and the instance key, and a Key Attestation is over the nonce"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sent and attests only keys sent; their signatures are the issuer’s to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"verify."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Failures reach the wallet as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WalletError"},{"type":"text","text":"s: one the network or the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"provider’s availability caused (no connection, a timeout, HTTP 5xx or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"429, a challenge that expired before it was used, App Attest’s server"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"unavailable) as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".network"},{"type":"text","text":", which may be retried"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/oid4vcwallet.OID4VCWallet\/documentation\/OID4VCWallet\/WalletProviderUnavailableError"},{"type":"text","text":"); a refusal"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/oid4vcwallet.OID4VCWallet\/documentation\/OID4VCWallet\/WalletProviderRefusedError"},{"type":"text","text":") as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".platform"},{"type":"text","text":", its message naming the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"protocol’s error code. On "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"instance_revoked"},{"type":"text","text":", it forgets the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"registration and deletes its registration key: the next Wallet"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Attestation registers the installation again. The revoked instance’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"instance keys stay its own ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"instance_key_registered"},{"type":"text","text":"), so a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"credential whose refresh needs one must be received again. On"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"instance_not_active"},{"type":"text","text":" (suspended) it keeps the registration: tell the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"holder, as the provider may resume it. A signed request refused as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"invalid_signed_request"},{"type":"text","text":" isn’t retried: check the device’s clock, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that the provider still knows the instance."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/oid4vcwallet\/httpwalletprovider"]}],"references":{"doc://oid4vcwallet.OID4VCWallet/documentation/OID4VCWallet/InstanceRegistry":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/oid4vcwallet.OID4VCWallet\/documentation\/OID4VCWallet\/InstanceRegistry","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"InstanceRegistry","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"InstanceRegistry","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Where ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/oid4vcwallet.OID4VCWallet\/documentation\/OID4VCWallet\/HttpWalletProvider","type":"reference"},{"text":" keeps the wallet’s registration, so the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"installation registers once, across launches. An instance ID isn’t a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"secret — every request naming it is signed with the registration key","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"— but losing it loses the instance: the wallet then registers again,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with a new registration key and App Attest key, and the instance keys","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the lost instance recorded can’t be attested again.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/oid4vcwallet.OID4